  closing:(s,all,G)=>{const cut=s.flags.cutregression, auto=s.flags.r_autonomy, p=s.picks||{};
    return [
    `Monday, November 21. Page seven came in the mail on a gray afternoon with a Golden postmark, and the first snow of the season blowing sideways across the porch in Aurora. He read it at the kitchen table with his coat still on.`,
    `<b>MAR 21 0930 ADMINISTRATOR ON THE LOOP: GOOD CALL, RUTHIE.</b>`,
    (cut
      ?`He knew what good call felt like. He'd felt it on Friday, November 4, at about a quarter to three, when the squad demoed nearly everything and the room liked it. He'd felt the other thing the Wednesday after, when the full suite finally ran and found the safe mode's wake timer a cycle late, from a change two files over that nobody had re-tested. He read Roz Tate's line at 0740 four times. She'd asked if anyone had rerun the abort sequence. The software lead said it didn't change. Then Tate again. THE THING NEXT TO IT DID.`
      :p[9]===3
        ?`He read the 0715 line four times. APPROVED NEW TESTS ONLY. REGRESSION DEFERRED TO DROP 8. MY INITIALS. On November 3 he'd had his own version of that line, with smaller numbers in it, and Yusra had taken stories out of the sprint instead, and the squad had shown twenty five points to a room that wanted thirty two. It hadn't felt like a good call. It had felt like a Thursday.`
        :p[9]===1
          ?`He read the 0715 line four times. APPROVED NEW TESTS ONLY. REGRESSION DEFERRED TO DROP 8. MY INITIALS. On November 3 he hadn't cut anything. He'd moved the review to the next Wednesday instead, and the regression had run by then, and A2-3 had paid for it with three days. He thought about Roz Tate at 0740, asking whether anyone had rerun the abort sequence, and putting it in writing because she was told to, and her note going into a file for drop 8.`
        :`He read the 0715 line four times. APPROVED NEW TESTS ONLY. REGRESSION DEFERRED TO DROP 8. MY INITIALS. On November 3 the regression had run, one way or another, and the squad had paid for it one way or another. He thought about Roz Tate at 0740, asking whether anyone had rerun the abort sequence, and putting it in writing because she was told to, and her note going into a file for drop 8.`),
    (p[8]===0
      ?`The board's November minutes had a paragraph on the defect under the program's report, and a line at the end of it in the board's capitals: THE BOARD NOTES THAT THE PROGRAM'S REPORT WAS RECEIVED BEFORE ANY INQUIRY.`
      :p[8]===1
        ?`The squad's tracker still said CONSTANT ERROR, FIXED. He'd stopped looking at it the way you stop looking at a gauge that reads fine.`
        :p[8]===2
          ?`Furrow was still grayed out in every toolbar in the squad. The rewrite had eaten all of A2-3. In one hand typed test fixture somebody had put 9.81, from memory, and Thandi's team had found it on November 17, and nobody had known what to say about that.`
          :`The engineer who'd accepted the routine had stopped asking questions at standup. Sam had noticed on the twelfth day, which was eleven days late.`),
    (p[10]===1
      ?`Tallgrass's software standard was at revision 12. Three other programs in the building had asked for the page, and one of them had found a constant of its own.`
      :``),
    (p[5]===0
      ?`Yusra's card was still at the top of the governance column. CRITERIA FOR AN UNCREWED DEPARTURE. By Thanksgiving she'd written four of them with her crew, at her kitchen table in Aurora, and sent them to the board for its December session. The first one said: Only if no crew can go.`
      :`Yusra ordered the backlog well, and she hadn't asked him anything that wasn't about the backlog since a Saturday in October. He'd started to notice the shape of that.`),
    (p[6]===3
      ?`Ada's answer had come on October 19. <span class="said" data-who="Ada" data-tone="Warm, relieved, a little unsteady.">"Malik called his mom. He said she asked him how he was, and then she waited, and he told her. He's still coughing. She's still on Earth. But he's less alone with it, and so am I, and I didn't break a promise. Thanks for not making me."</span>`
      :p[6]===0
        ?`Ada's logs since October 19 had been about the night bays and the pumps, and Malik hadn't been in any of them.`
        :p[6]===1
          ?`Frances had called back in the second week of November to ask which of the two things he'd told her she should believe. He'd told her the truth then. It was three weeks late, and she'd noticed.`
          :`Frances hadn't called again. Ada said Malik had a message from his mother that started with Hollis Bayne's name, and that he hadn't answered it yet.`),
    (auto
      ?`On Quinn's integrated plan there was a milestone that hadn't been there in September, a diamond with a dashed line and the word OPTION beside it in capitals, Hana's word. `+(p[7]===2?`Release A2, most likely February 24, range February 10 to March 10.`:p[7]===1?`Release A2, February 24.`:p[7]===0?`Release A2, the end of January, the date Hale had given the partners.`:`Release A2, and no date beside it.`)+` It was the only thing on the plan that existed in case.`
      :p[1]===1
        ?`Quinn's sticky note had fallen behind his desk. He hadn't looked for it. WHAT IF THE CREW CAN'T GO.`
        :p[1]===0
          ?`The uncrewed work was in the backlog, near the top, ordered well, and still not in the integrated plan. Quinn had a milestone drawn for it in pencil.`
          :`The Director had said could in October, and the feed had said can, and ever since the partners had asked at every meeting about the ship that flew itself, which had flown its departure twice.`),
    `Thursday, November 24. Thanksgiving. He'd been asked to three houses and gone to none of them. At eight he sat at the kitchen table with a plate from the grocery store's hot counter and pressed record. One way light time fifteen minutes and thirty seconds. He told her about page seven, and Field 6, and the gravity constant, which she'd appreciate, because at twelve she'd lost a science fair to a units error and cried about it in the car all the way home.`,
    (s.score>=27
      ?`He told her it had been a good two months, mostly, and then he told her the parts that hadn't been, because she'd ask.`
      :`He told her the calls he'd make differently, in order. He could name them now without looking at his notebook. Ray would have said that was a start, and then asked what he planned to do about the next one.`),
    `He didn't do the voice. He sent it, and fifteen minutes and thirty seconds later it was on Mars.`,
    `Monday, November 28. 8:05 AM. Peg Sato from contracts came into his office without knocking, which she'd never done, put a folder on his desk, and sat down, which she'd also never done.`,
    `The folder was Aldergrove Fluid Systems blue, with the Pueblo address on the label. Inside was a letter on the company's letterhead, signed by Nell Garrity, requesting a change to the valve contract.`,
    `<span class="said" data-who="Peg">"Aldergrove wants the root cause work pulled out of their fixed price. They put a number on it. I've read the number twice, once sitting down."</span> She folded her glasses and set them on the folder. <span class="said" data-who="Peg">"Garrett called me at six. He'd like to fire them."</span>`,
    `Sam opened the folder. Under the letter somebody at Aldergrove had clipped a photocopy of a page from 2034, cold cycle data in faded columns, and beside the third row, in Nell's handwriting, two words: <b>Still asking.</b> He closed it again and put his hand flat on the cover, the way Quinn did, and thought about who in the building he had to talk to first. It wasn't Garrett.`,
    `Over the high bay doors the countdown clock said 447. In the morning it would say 446, folder or no folder.`
  ].filter(x=>x!==``);},
